WEBVTT

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.908
The Devore ships are assuming
a tactical formation.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.137
Bridge to Transporter Room.
Status?

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.179
All set here, Captain.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.611
Pattern cohesion looks stable.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.273
Cargo Bay 1, report.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.611
The bay is clear.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.242
They're powering weapons.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.251
Why do they bother?

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.651
They know we won't resist.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.484
Protocol, Mr. Paris.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:25.817
They're hailing.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:31.156
Gaharay vessel,
prepare to be inspected.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.823
Crew members are instructed

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.366
to step away
from their stations.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.696
We know the drill.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:38.567
Side arms and scanning equipment
are to be set aside.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.969
Deviation from this

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.907
or any other inspection
protocols will not be tolerated.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:45.740
All hands, this is the Captain.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.645
Prepare to be boarded
by Devore inspection teams.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.342
Give them your full cooperation.

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.214
Let's get this over with.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:58.815
Their soldiers have materialized
on Decks 15, 11, 4 and 1.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.996
Captain Janeway,
report to your ready room.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.938
Good morning, Captain.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:15.338
I took the liberty
of playing this music

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.636
throughout your ship.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.177
I thought it might help
your crew relax.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:22.646
Sometimes these inspections
can be stressful.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.307
How thoughtful.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:27.945
I've replicated some coffee.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.010
Black, as usual?

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.482
Black.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:36.461
Prax here still refuses
to try it,

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:40.693
but then, he's a man
of few pleasures.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.968
Captain,
please make yourself at home.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.798
Those cell cultures
are extremely fragile.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.998
Please...

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.285
You've been routing power
through your transporter system.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.786
Why?

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.117
It's a routine diagnostic.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.521
We've been having trouble
with our imaging scanners.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.390
The problem is in the primary
energizing coils.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.224
Focus your efforts there.

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:02.059
Thanks for the tip.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.152
Contaminated antimatter.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.714
This material could interfere
with our readings.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.423
A bionetic implant?

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.692
An interlink node.

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:36.701
It permits communication
with other Borg drones.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.202
You are not a telepath.

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:40.262
No.

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:45.072
Remarkable.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.441
How old is this?

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.706
About 600 years.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.578
My grandfather gave it
to me when I was a child.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:53.278
It seems you have
a long-standing obsession

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:54.945
with exploration, Captain.

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:58.489
I, on the other hand,
have much more in common

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.526
with this ancient soldier.

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:02.322
He's from Earth's
classical period.

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:04.886
It produced some of our
greatest artists as well.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:08.900
Your culture has
many contradictions.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:12.732
Violence and beauty,
science and faith...

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:15.899
all somehow mingled
harmoniously.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:18.135
Like the counterpoint
of this music.

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:20.406
Mahler, Symphony #1.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.913
Am I correct?

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:22.913
You're getting to know

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.449
my musical database
better than I do.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.917
I've had time to review it
since our last encounter.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:29.386
Tell me, are all of your
inspections this personal?

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.616
I'm just trying to get
to know you, Captain.

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:33.818
There's no reason for us
to be adversaries.

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:35.224
I could be your friend

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.922
and, right now,
you could certainly use one.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.760
Really? Why is that?

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:41.163
Your predicament.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:44.203
I don't expect it's been easy.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:47.603
Thousands of light-years
from home,

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:49.732
navigating by strange stars,

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:52.471
trespassing
in other people's space,

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:54.342
ignoring their laws.

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:56.348
We're just trying
to get back to Earth, Inspector.

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:57.815
Through the Devore lmperium?

00:06:57.884 --> 00:06:59.408
It's tough to avoid.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.350
Still, most people
make the effort.

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:03.321
We don't exactly embrace
outsiders.

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:04.822
"Gaharay."

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:07.382
It means "strangers."

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.360
Which brings me to a matter

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:12.296
that could threaten
our friendship.

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:18.531
I've examined your crew manifest
from our last inspection.

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:22.836
Commander Tuvok, Ensign Vorik...
Vulcans.

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:25.173
Ensigns Suder and Jurot...
Betazoids.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.711
All telepaths...

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:30.180
and yet for some reason,
you neglected to mention them.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:31.910
For a very simple reason.

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:33.313
They're dead.

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:35.911
Tuvok, Vorik and Jurot
died in a shuttle crash

00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:37.455
about two months ago.

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:41.220
Suder was killed in a conflict
with a species called the Kazon.

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:42.886
That's fortunate...

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:44.395
for you, I mean.

00:07:44.464 --> 00:07:46.329
If I'd found you
were harboring telepaths,

00:07:46.399 --> 00:07:48.663
I would have had to arrest you

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.929
for breaking
our Cardinal Protocol.

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:53.835
They were valued members
of my crew, Inspector,

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:55.168
not criminals.

00:07:55.241 --> 00:07:57.232
Perhaps.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.938
Captain...

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:01.843
do you trust me?

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:02.972
Not for a second.

00:08:03.049 --> 00:08:04.448
Exactly.

00:08:04.517 --> 00:08:05.882
And why should you?

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:07.713
Trust has to be earned.

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:09.277
It's gradual,

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:12.119
and yet it's the foundation
of every relationship,

00:08:12.191 --> 00:08:14.284
professional and personal.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:19.525
It's also a concept
alien to the telepathic races.

00:08:19.599 --> 00:08:21.430
Why take someone at their word

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:23.696
when you can simply read
their mind?

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:26.767
We've completed our inspection.

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:28.602
There are no telepaths aboard.

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:31.575
However, their sensor logs
indicate they deviated

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:34.272
from their assigned
course on two occasions.

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:37.874
In both cases,
to avoid ion storms.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:42.546
Imperative 32, Codicil 626:

00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:44.249
"All gaharay vessels.

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:46.314
"That deviate
from prescribed flight vectors

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:48.917
will be impounded, their crews
detained and relocated."

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:50.428
Prax, it's clear

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:53.590
the Captain didn't
intend to break protocol.

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:56.464
I expect we can overlook
these infractions.

00:08:56.536 --> 00:08:57.628
Sir?

00:09:00.706 --> 00:09:01.638
Yes, sir.

00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:06.269
Captain, I'm a reasonable man

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:10.441
and you've been cooperative,
but consider this a reminder.

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:13.280
You have a long trip
through Devore space

00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:15.547
and good friends
can be an asset.

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:18.215
I'll keep it in mind.

00:09:33.906 --> 00:09:35.897
The Devore vessels are
out of range.

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:39.172
Bridge to Transporter Team.
You're clear.

00:09:43.516 --> 00:09:45.814
Cargo Bay 1 to Ensign Kim.

00:09:45.885 --> 00:09:47.785
Pattern enhancers are in place.

00:09:48.988 --> 00:09:52.014
Initiating rematerialization
sequence.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:55.083
Harry, I'm routing maximum power
to the transporters.

00:09:56.696 --> 00:09:58.493
Got it.

00:09:58.564 --> 00:10:01.761
Align the confinement
beam to ten angstroms.

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.529
Energizing.

00:10:06.172 --> 00:10:09.471
Ensign Kim, the confinement beam
is unstable.

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:11.134
We're trying to correct it now.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.507
What's the problem?

00:10:12.578 --> 00:10:15.138
We're unable to consolidate
their patterns.

00:10:15.214 --> 00:10:17.273
They've been
in suspension too long.

00:10:18.651 --> 00:10:21.814
Harry, increase power
to the imaging scanners.

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:22.876
Aye, Captain.

00:10:24.957 --> 00:10:26.447
It's working.

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:48.507
Nice work, Harry.

00:10:48.581 --> 00:10:50.947
All our guests are present
and accounted for.

00:10:51.017 --> 00:10:52.109
Captain...

00:10:52.184 --> 00:10:54.084
They're gone... for now.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.187
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:11:03.262 --> 00:11:05.230
After weeks
of playing hide-and-seek

00:11:05.297 --> 00:11:08.164
with the Devore inspectors,
our goal is near...

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:10.828
a transport vessel
that will take our passengers

00:11:10.903 --> 00:11:13.736
to a wormhole leading
out of hostile territory.

00:11:15.508 --> 00:11:16.941
Back to your old self again?

00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:18.737
Each time we do this,
I feel as though I've left

00:11:18.811 --> 00:11:20.711
a few molecules behind
in your cargo bay.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.077
Well, I'll have someone
scan the room

00:11:22.148 --> 00:11:23.376
if it'll make you feel better.

00:11:23.449 --> 00:11:24.939
Kir, we just received
an encoded message

00:11:25.017 --> 00:11:26.177
from the transport vessel.

00:11:26.252 --> 00:11:28.117
They've changed the
rendezvous point again.

00:11:28.187 --> 00:11:29.154
I'm afraid so.

00:11:29.221 --> 00:11:30.848
Did they send
the new coordinates?

00:11:30.923 --> 00:11:32.322
We're still waiting for them.

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:34.450
Captain, we may have
another problem.

00:11:34.527 --> 00:11:36.961
I just treated Tuvok
and two of the refugees

00:11:37.029 --> 00:11:38.690
for acute cellular degradation.

00:11:38.764 --> 00:11:40.891
I've repaired
most of the damage,

00:11:40.966 --> 00:11:42.957
but unfortunately,
the effect is cumulative.

00:11:43.035 --> 00:11:43.967
Meaning?

00:11:44.103 --> 00:11:46.867
If we continue to go
into transporter suspension,

00:11:46.939 --> 00:11:48.167
some of us may not survive.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.174
Bridge to Captain Janeway.

00:11:50.242 --> 00:11:51.174
Go ahead.

00:11:51.243 --> 00:11:52.505
We're receiving
another transmission.

00:11:52.578 --> 00:11:53.545
Acknowledged.

00:11:56.649 --> 00:11:58.276
The new coordinates are here

00:11:58.350 --> 00:11:59.908
within a Mutara-class nebula,

00:11:59.985 --> 00:12:02.249
2.36 light-years
from our current position.

00:12:02.321 --> 00:12:04.016
It's definitely out of the way...

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:05.580
less chance
of being discovered...

00:12:05.658 --> 00:12:07.717
but it'll take
two more days to get there.

00:12:07.793 --> 00:12:09.693
Two days...
that increases the chances

00:12:09.762 --> 00:12:11.730
that we'll run
into another inspection.

00:12:11.797 --> 00:12:13.731
Given the frequency
of patrols in that area,

00:12:13.799 --> 00:12:15.664
it's likely we'll be
stopped at least once.

00:12:15.735 --> 00:12:17.327
Just what the Doctor
didn't order.

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:19.303
Tuvok, Seven, I want you
to lay in a course

00:12:19.371 --> 00:12:21.601
that'll attract
as little attention as possible.

00:12:21.674 --> 00:12:23.835
We'll avoid their colonies,
space stations,

00:12:23.909 --> 00:12:26.400
tourist attractions...
if they have any.

00:12:28.147 --> 00:12:31.344
The Ogre of Fire's castle
hovered over the forest

00:12:31.417 --> 00:12:34.875
like a great, black spaceship,
turning day into night.

00:12:34.954 --> 00:12:38.355
Now, Flotter and Trevis
knew they had to find a way

00:12:38.424 --> 00:12:40.449
to keep the Ogre from
burning the forest down,

00:12:40.526 --> 00:12:44.292
but his castle... it was
higher than the tallest tree.

00:12:44.363 --> 00:12:47.389
It seemed hopeless
until they discovered...

00:12:47.466 --> 00:12:48.398
A door.

00:12:48.467 --> 00:12:49.627
A door, right.

00:12:49.702 --> 00:12:53.138
A mysterious door,
right in the middle of a...

00:12:53.205 --> 00:12:54.604
The clearing.

00:12:54.673 --> 00:12:56.072
You know, it's...

00:12:56.142 --> 00:12:58.372
it's not nice
to read people's thoughts

00:12:58.444 --> 00:13:00.309
when they're telling a story.

00:13:00.379 --> 00:13:02.108
I'm sorry.

00:13:02.181 --> 00:13:03.409
It's all right.

00:13:06.986 --> 00:13:09.614
Why don't you all go play
by yourselves for a while?

00:13:09.688 --> 00:13:11.212
We'll finish the story later.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:15.457
How are they doing?

00:13:15.528 --> 00:13:16.927
Oh, fine, more or less.

00:13:16.996 --> 00:13:19.897
They don't understand
what all the fuss is about,

00:13:19.965 --> 00:13:21.933
but they're telepaths, Captain.

00:13:22.001 --> 00:13:24.435
If the parents are
concerned or fearful,

00:13:24.503 --> 00:13:27.267
the children feel it, too.

00:13:27.339 --> 00:13:28.636
You did the right thing.

00:13:28.707 --> 00:13:30.902
If we hadn't taken them
off that freighter,

00:13:30.976 --> 00:13:33.035
they'd be in a detention
center by now.

00:13:33.112 --> 00:13:35.842
Well, we're going to make sure
that doesn't happen.

00:13:35.915 --> 00:13:37.940
Is the kitchen still open

00:13:38.083 --> 00:13:40.643
or are you just serving stories?

00:13:40.719 --> 00:13:43.017
For you, it's always open.

00:13:45.591 --> 00:13:47.218
Commander,
I'm detecting a vessel,

00:13:47.293 --> 00:13:48.851
300,000 kilometers and closing.

00:13:48.928 --> 00:13:50.122
The signature is Devore.

00:13:50.196 --> 00:13:52.494
Red Alert. Shields up.

00:13:52.565 --> 00:13:54.624
Bridge to Captain.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:55.724
More company, Commander?

00:13:55.801 --> 00:13:56.768
Looks like it.

00:13:56.836 --> 00:13:58.428
Get our visitors
to the cargo bay.

00:13:58.504 --> 00:14:00.267
Stand by
for transporter suspension.

00:14:00.339 --> 00:14:01.772
Aye, Captain.

00:14:01.841 --> 00:14:02.773
Neelix.

00:14:02.842 --> 00:14:03.774
Right away.

00:14:03.843 --> 00:14:04.901
Come on, now.

00:14:04.977 --> 00:14:07.070
We're going to go
see your parents.

00:14:07.146 --> 00:14:08.545
Let's go.

00:14:09.982 --> 00:14:11.244
Report.

00:14:11.317 --> 00:14:13.911
It's a scout ship.
One pilot; no other crew.

00:14:14.019 --> 00:14:16.817
The vessel hasn't raised shields
or charged weapons.

00:14:16.889 --> 00:14:18.254
If this is another inspection,

00:14:18.324 --> 00:14:19.916
it's certainly
a different approach.

00:14:20.059 --> 00:14:21.151
We're being hailed.

00:14:21.227 --> 00:14:22.717
Open a channel.

00:14:23.429 --> 00:14:24.828
Captain.

00:14:24.897 --> 00:14:26.455
Inspector.

00:14:26.532 --> 00:14:27.726
It's urgent that we speak.

00:14:29.335 --> 00:14:31.701
You know the way
to my ready room.

00:14:39.011 --> 00:14:41.104
It's all right, Ensign.

00:14:44.483 --> 00:14:46.542
I submitted
to your previous inspections

00:14:46.619 --> 00:14:47.677
because you outgunned me,

00:14:47.753 --> 00:14:49.687
but I don't see
any of your warships nearby.

00:14:49.755 --> 00:14:51.552
I have no intention
of cooperating.

00:14:51.624 --> 00:14:54.092
I'm not here to search Voyager.

00:14:54.159 --> 00:14:56.184
Then what do you want,
inspector?

00:14:56.262 --> 00:14:58.287
Call me Kashyk, please.

00:14:58.364 --> 00:15:00.525
I never liked that title.

00:15:00.599 --> 00:15:03.067
In fact, I've left it behind.

00:15:03.135 --> 00:15:04.898
Did somebody offer you

00:15:05.004 --> 00:15:07.768
a promotion, or are you
just having a bad day?

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:11.503
I'm defecting,
and I need your help.

00:15:11.577 --> 00:15:13.272
Me?

00:15:13.345 --> 00:15:17.611
I've come to ask asylum...
safe passage out of Devore space

00:15:17.683 --> 00:15:21.016
before I end up
in a detention center myself.

00:15:21.086 --> 00:15:25.113
Now, why would I risk
the safety of my crew

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:27.522
by harboring a defector?

00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:29.720
Because of what
I'm about to tell you.

00:15:29.795 --> 00:15:33.231
If you continue
on your present course,

00:15:33.299 --> 00:15:36.234
you'll be intercepted
by a squadron of my warships.

00:15:36.302 --> 00:15:40.238
Voyager will be seized,
your crew imprisoned or worse.

00:15:40.306 --> 00:15:43.537
The nebula is a trap, Captain,

00:15:43.609 --> 00:15:47.045
to catch vessels
smuggling telepaths.

00:15:47.112 --> 00:15:50.081
You've inspected my ship
three times.

00:15:50.149 --> 00:15:53.915
You know we aren't smuggling
telepaths or anyone else.

00:15:53.986 --> 00:15:57.786
What I know is that you have
12 refugees aboard right now,

00:15:57.856 --> 00:16:01.053
that you rescued them
from a freighter three weeks ago

00:16:01.126 --> 00:16:03.026
and that you've
been concealing them

00:16:03.095 --> 00:16:05.222
in Cargo Bay 1,
using your transporters.

00:16:05.297 --> 00:16:06.457
I could have exposed them

00:16:06.532 --> 00:16:09.865
at any time, but I wanted them
to escape as much as you do.

00:16:09.935 --> 00:16:11.630
I can still protect them,

00:16:11.704 --> 00:16:13.729
but only if you
take me with you.

00:16:13.806 --> 00:16:17.401
My people know
about the wormhole.

00:16:17.476 --> 00:16:20.502
It's only a matter of time
before they find it.

00:16:23.315 --> 00:16:26.307
You have no choice, Captain.

00:16:26.385 --> 00:16:29.149
I'm your only hope.

00:16:41.967 --> 00:16:44.936
This is our rendezvous point
inside this nebula.

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:46.935
Unfortunately,
the transport vessel

00:16:47.006 --> 00:16:49.270
we're supposed to meet
is no longer there.

00:16:49.341 --> 00:16:50.467
Inspector.

00:16:56.715 --> 00:16:58.046
A Devore warship.

00:16:58.117 --> 00:16:59.243
One of a dozen

00:16:59.318 --> 00:17:00.945
positioned
throughout the nebula...

00:17:01.086 --> 00:17:02.553
all invisible to our sensors

00:17:02.621 --> 00:17:04.646
until Kashyk showed
me how to compensate

00:17:04.723 --> 00:17:06.350
for their refractive shielding.

00:17:06.425 --> 00:17:08.893
Your soldiers intercepted
the transport ship?

00:17:09.028 --> 00:17:10.188
Over a week ago.

00:17:10.262 --> 00:17:13.493
We were the ones who changed
the rendezvous coordinates.

00:17:13.565 --> 00:17:16.898
Two vessels carrying refugees
have already been seized.

00:17:17.002 --> 00:17:18.902
Voyager would have been next.

00:17:19.038 --> 00:17:20.266
All right, Inspector,

00:17:20.339 --> 00:17:22.569
you helped us avoid
this ambush. What now?

00:17:22.641 --> 00:17:24.268
We'll have to get
your passengers

00:17:24.343 --> 00:17:25.708
to the wormhole on our own.

00:17:25.778 --> 00:17:28.474
These are the schedules
and routes of our patrols,

00:17:28.547 --> 00:17:31.243
along with tactical
data on our shield

00:17:31.316 --> 00:17:33.250
and weapons configurations...
enough to ensure

00:17:33.318 --> 00:17:35.115
that you avoid
another inspection.

00:17:35.187 --> 00:17:36.711
How long before you're missed?

00:17:36.789 --> 00:17:38.347
Well, I took two weeks' leave.

00:17:38.424 --> 00:17:40.585
Enough time, I hope,
to find the wormhole

00:17:40.659 --> 00:17:42.820
and get your passengers
safely through it,

00:17:42.895 --> 00:17:44.556
and myself, as well.

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:45.756
Your data is useful,

00:17:45.831 --> 00:17:47.765
but it doesn't guarantee
our success.

00:17:47.833 --> 00:17:52.930
No. For that, you'll need
my guidance and some luck.

00:17:53.005 --> 00:17:55.599
I'll have to take this
up with the Brenari...

00:17:55.674 --> 00:17:58.199
see what they think
of their new benefactor.

00:17:58.277 --> 00:18:00.268
I'll let you know
what they decide.

00:18:00.345 --> 00:18:03.314
I'll have to insist
you remain under guard.

00:18:03.382 --> 00:18:06.283
- No hard feelings.
- No hard feelings.

00:18:09.321 --> 00:18:11.516
It's unusual...
but not unheard of.

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.888
There have been
sympathizers before.

00:18:13.959 --> 00:18:15.984
Kashyk may be telling the truth.

00:18:16.061 --> 00:18:17.460
Maybe you should
just read his thoughts.

00:18:17.529 --> 00:18:18.723
Devore soldiers undergo

00:18:18.797 --> 00:18:20.890
years of mental training
to prevent that.

00:18:21.033 --> 00:18:22.830
He might be telling the truth,

00:18:22.901 --> 00:18:25.870
but he also might be using us
to find the wormhole.

00:18:25.938 --> 00:18:28.805
So what do we do, throw
him in the brig?

00:18:28.874 --> 00:18:30.808
No.

00:18:30.876 --> 00:18:33.242
We take him up
on his offer to help,

00:18:33.312 --> 00:18:34.609
see how it plays out.

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:36.807
But I want
'round-the-clock security.

00:18:36.882 --> 00:18:38.873
We need to watch
his every movement.

00:18:38.951 --> 00:18:41.078
That leaves us with
our next question:

00:18:41.153 --> 00:18:43.144
How do we find the wormhole?

00:18:43.222 --> 00:18:44.689
I've given it some thought.

00:18:44.756 --> 00:18:46.519
There's a scientist named Torat.

00:18:46.592 --> 00:18:48.025
He's from a nearby system.

00:18:48.093 --> 00:18:51.256
He's rumored to know more
about the wormhole than anyone.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:54.299
He might help us... for a price.

00:18:54.366 --> 00:18:55.924
- A price?
- His species power

00:18:56.068 --> 00:18:58.662
their ships with a fluidic alloy
that's difficult to find.

00:18:58.737 --> 00:18:59.863
Perhaps we can replicate it.

00:18:59.938 --> 00:19:01.872
I have some data
on its composition.

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:03.032
See what you can do.

00:19:03.108 --> 00:19:04.302
In the meantime,

00:19:04.376 --> 00:19:06.367
we'll set a course
for Torat's planet,

00:19:06.445 --> 00:19:07.707
try to track him down.

00:19:16.054 --> 00:19:17.988
Nervous?

00:19:19.391 --> 00:19:21.018
Let's just say...

00:19:21.093 --> 00:19:24.256
I'm not used to other people
deciding my fate.

00:19:30.202 --> 00:19:33.262
Until today,
you were part of a government

00:19:33.338 --> 00:19:38.207
responsible for persecuting
thousands of innocent people.

00:19:38.277 --> 00:19:40.575
Why the sudden change of heart?

00:19:40.646 --> 00:19:42.409
There's nothing sudden about it.

00:19:42.481 --> 00:19:45.109
I've been looking
for a way to escape for years.

00:19:45.184 --> 00:19:47.175
Voyager was
the perfect opportunity.

00:19:47.252 --> 00:19:48.412
How so?

00:19:48.487 --> 00:19:50.250
Well, what are you suggesting...

00:19:50.322 --> 00:19:52.381
I ask a Brenari vessel
for assistance?

00:19:52.457 --> 00:19:54.186
They'd throw me out an airlock.

00:19:54.259 --> 00:19:56.352
Besides...

00:19:56.428 --> 00:19:59.886
you're something
of a humanitarian, Captain.

00:19:59.965 --> 00:20:01.592
I've read your database.

00:20:01.667 --> 00:20:04.227
I know all about
Starfleet philosophy,

00:20:04.303 --> 00:20:06.669
unless you left
those ideals behind

00:20:06.738 --> 00:20:08.262
in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:11.901
I certainly don't grant asylum
to every person I meet,

00:20:11.977 --> 00:20:14.241
especially ones
who ransack my ship

00:20:14.313 --> 00:20:16.304
and terrorize my crew.

00:20:16.381 --> 00:20:20.841
You're asking me to believe
you're someone else...

00:20:20.919 --> 00:20:26.050
and... that's a leap of
faith I'm not ready to make.

00:20:26.124 --> 00:20:28.285
You're turning me away.

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:29.554
No.

00:20:31.029 --> 00:20:32.053
No.

00:20:33.565 --> 00:20:36.830
I'm going to give you safe
passage to the wormhole...

00:20:36.902 --> 00:20:39.700
in return for your help
in getting us there,

00:20:39.771 --> 00:20:42.296
but I'm also imposing
some restrictions.

00:20:42.374 --> 00:20:44.274
You'll have your own quarters,

00:20:44.343 --> 00:20:46.971
but limited access
to Voyager's systems,

00:20:47.045 --> 00:20:50.606
and your whereabouts will
be monitored at all times.

00:20:50.682 --> 00:20:53.810
I'm used to being surrounded
by armed guards.

00:20:53.885 --> 00:20:55.512
Makes me feel secure.

00:20:57.155 --> 00:20:59.453
Only this time,
they answer to me.

00:20:59.524 --> 00:21:02.925
Consider them a reminder
that Voyager is my ship.

00:21:03.028 --> 00:21:05.519
I don't think anyone
could doubt that.

00:21:18.343 --> 00:21:20.174
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:21:20.245 --> 00:21:22.179
It's taken us nearly two days,

00:21:22.247 --> 00:21:24.442
but we've managed
to locate Torat,

00:21:24.516 --> 00:21:27.576
the man who's supposedly
an expert on wormholes.

00:21:27.653 --> 00:21:29.746
Unfortunately,
he seems reluctant

00:21:29.821 --> 00:21:31.311
to share his expertise.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:32.857
He's trying to evade us.

00:21:32.924 --> 00:21:34.050
Hail him again.

00:21:34.126 --> 00:21:35.923
Mr. Torat doesn't
seem too trusting.

00:21:35.994 --> 00:21:38.485
Maybe he's been through
one inspection too many.

00:21:38.563 --> 00:21:39.928
No response.

00:21:39.998 --> 00:21:42.660
He's deactivated
his communications system.

00:21:42.734 --> 00:21:45.464
I think I can tap into his
computer, override the lockout.

00:21:45.537 --> 00:21:46.504
Do it.

00:21:51.109 --> 00:21:52.872
Go away!

00:21:54.079 --> 00:21:55.706
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:21:55.781 --> 00:21:57.749
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:21:57.816 --> 00:21:59.215
We have no hostile intent.

00:21:59.284 --> 00:22:01.149
Then why are you pursuing me?

00:22:01.219 --> 00:22:02.151
We'd just like to ask...

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:04.620
Federations, lmperiums...

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:07.352
Why do you people
feel such a need

00:22:07.426 --> 00:22:11.487
to align yourselves with
monolithic organizations, hmm?

00:22:11.563 --> 00:22:12.552
I'd be glad to discuss that

00:22:12.631 --> 00:22:14.599
and any other philosophical
issue you care to raise,

00:22:14.666 --> 00:22:17.032
if you would just
slow down and talk.

00:22:17.102 --> 00:22:18.399
Sorry. Can't do that.

00:22:18.470 --> 00:22:21.769
I'm late
for a very important conference!

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:24.104
This is a waste of time.
Disable his ship.

00:22:24.176 --> 00:22:26.076
That's what we call
overkill, Inspector.

00:22:26.144 --> 00:22:27.907
Ensign, can we transport
at this range?

00:22:27.979 --> 00:22:30.243
Absolutely. Energizing.

00:22:35.387 --> 00:22:36.786
Welcome aboard.

00:22:36.855 --> 00:22:39.085
Your reputation precedes you.

00:22:43.095 --> 00:22:46.826
20 centiliters of mercurium
isochromate... no impurities...

00:22:46.898 --> 00:22:48.456
and this is just a sample.

00:22:48.533 --> 00:22:52.731
We've synthesized enough
to power your ship for a year.

00:22:52.804 --> 00:22:54.135
It doesn't matter.

00:22:54.206 --> 00:22:57.334
I never heard of this...
wormhole you're looking for,

00:22:57.409 --> 00:22:58.967
or these so-called refugees.

00:22:59.044 --> 00:23:00.568
Well, they've heard of you.

00:23:00.645 --> 00:23:02.875
Well, no doubt...
my research is famous.

00:23:02.948 --> 00:23:05.416
Think of all the stars
you could research

00:23:05.484 --> 00:23:08.681
once you've infused your
propulsion system with this.

00:23:08.754 --> 00:23:10.585
There's no point in bribing me.

00:23:10.655 --> 00:23:14.284
He's right. He couldn't
help us if he wanted to.

00:23:14.359 --> 00:23:15.758
What do you mean by that?

00:23:15.827 --> 00:23:19.319
I doubt you'd know a wormhole
from a dark matter inversion.

00:23:19.398 --> 00:23:21.662
Professor... Kashyk
is another expert

00:23:21.733 --> 00:23:24.293
I've retained to help
us with this matter.

00:23:24.369 --> 00:23:25.529
I'm afraid he's not

00:23:25.604 --> 00:23:27.834
as impressed with your work
as I am.

00:23:27.906 --> 00:23:30.841
In fact, he discouraged me
from seeking you out.

00:23:30.909 --> 00:23:34.345
Professor Kashyk?
Never heard of you.

00:23:34.413 --> 00:23:35.607
Not surprising,

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:38.114
considering you toil
in scientific obscurity.

00:23:38.183 --> 00:23:40.708
Obscurity?!

00:23:40.786 --> 00:23:43.949
I-I've discovered over 60
astronomical phenomena!

00:23:44.022 --> 00:23:47.185
Not worth the sensors
they were recorded on.

00:23:47.259 --> 00:23:48.226
Oh...

00:23:48.293 --> 00:23:49.954
There's no need
to insult the man.

00:23:50.095 --> 00:23:53.587
Just because he doesn't know how
to find an interspatial flexure.

00:23:53.665 --> 00:23:55.132
Interspatial flexure?

00:23:55.200 --> 00:23:57.794
Why didn't you say so
in the first place?

00:23:57.869 --> 00:24:00.702
He said wormhole...
a layman's term

00:24:00.772 --> 00:24:03.764
that... that covers
any number of phenomena.

00:24:03.842 --> 00:24:06.276
I am familiar
with a certain anomaly

00:24:06.344 --> 00:24:10.872
that could be categorized
as an "interspatial flexure."

00:24:10.949 --> 00:24:13.144
Where is it?

00:24:13.218 --> 00:24:15.186
Actually,
a better question would be:

00:24:15.253 --> 00:24:16.550
Where is it now?

00:24:16.621 --> 00:24:18.452
It's really quite interesting.

00:24:18.523 --> 00:24:20.491
The aperture of the phenomenon...

00:24:20.559 --> 00:24:21.924
which I prefer to call

00:24:21.993 --> 00:24:24.826
an intermittent
cyclical vortex... is unfixed.

00:24:24.896 --> 00:24:26.488
It manifests infrequently,

00:24:26.565 --> 00:24:29.796
for only brief periods of time
and in varying locations.

00:24:37.075 --> 00:24:39.543
I can give you
the last four locations.

00:24:39.611 --> 00:24:42.341
Perhaps you can extrapolate
the next one...

00:24:42.414 --> 00:24:46.817
if you're as accomplished
a scientist as you claim to be.

00:24:54.292 --> 00:24:55.384
- Think.
- I'm thinking.

00:24:55.460 --> 00:24:57.052
Think harder.
Four wormhole appearances

00:24:57.128 --> 00:24:59.358
less than 20 light-years apart...
there's no pattern.

00:24:59.431 --> 00:25:00.921
Did you apply
a fractal coefficient?

00:25:00.999 --> 00:25:01.931
Didn't work.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:02.898
Neutrino flux parameters?

00:25:03.001 --> 00:25:03.899
Mm-hmm.

00:25:04.002 --> 00:25:04.900
Statistical algorithms?

00:25:05.036 --> 00:25:06.333
Every one I could find.

00:25:06.404 --> 00:25:07.894
This wormhole defies analysis.

00:25:08.006 --> 00:25:09.132
Maybe Torat was right...

00:25:09.207 --> 00:25:10.697
we're just out of our league.

00:25:10.775 --> 00:25:12.299
It's not like you to give up.

00:25:12.377 --> 00:25:13.309
Think harder.

00:25:13.378 --> 00:25:15.141
How do you predict...

00:25:15.213 --> 00:25:17.113
a random occurrence?

00:25:17.182 --> 00:25:19.707
You follow your instincts.

00:25:23.021 --> 00:25:24.318
Captain?

00:25:26.224 --> 00:25:28.055
Counterpoint.

00:25:28.126 --> 00:25:29.889
It's in all great music.

00:25:29.961 --> 00:25:32.930
Parallel melodies
playing against one another.

00:25:32.998 --> 00:25:34.795
We've been looking
at the obvious...

00:25:34.866 --> 00:25:37.926
frequency, location, timing...
but each of those parameters

00:25:38.036 --> 00:25:40.027
could have a counterpoint
in subspace.

00:25:40.105 --> 00:25:43.233
If we could run an algorithm
based on subspace harmonics,

00:25:43.308 --> 00:25:44.866
it might reveal our pattern.

00:25:44.943 --> 00:25:47.741
Computer, run a subspatial
transkinetic analysis

00:25:47.812 --> 00:25:49.302
on the wormhole data.

00:25:49.381 --> 00:25:50.814
Analysis in progress.

00:25:50.882 --> 00:25:52.509
This'll take a minute.

00:25:58.890 --> 00:26:01.688
I'm going to miss this...
coffee of yours.

00:26:01.760 --> 00:26:03.853
Well, I will give you
the recipe.

00:26:03.929 --> 00:26:05.362
Thank you.

00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:07.898
You don't sound
too happy about leaving.

00:26:07.999 --> 00:26:11.526
The Brenari aren't about
to embrace a former Inspector.

00:26:11.603 --> 00:26:14.595
I'll be feared,
hated for what I represent.

00:26:14.673 --> 00:26:16.903
Anxiety doesn't
become you, Inspector.

00:26:17.008 --> 00:26:18.236
Try to relax a little.

00:26:18.310 --> 00:26:20.608
I suppose you liked me better
in uniform.

00:26:20.679 --> 00:26:24.342
I haven't decided
whether I like you at all.

00:26:31.656 --> 00:26:36.650
We call them the Kolyan Kolyar...
Infinite Spirals.

00:26:36.728 --> 00:26:38.195
Beautiful.

00:26:38.263 --> 00:26:42.393
As a boy, I spent years
gazing at these lights.

00:26:42.467 --> 00:26:45.265
This is the last time
I'll ever see them.

00:26:45.337 --> 00:26:47.931
We have something
similar back on Earth...

00:26:48.006 --> 00:26:49.268
the Aurora Borealis.

00:26:49.341 --> 00:26:51.434
Which you, too,
may never see again.

00:26:51.509 --> 00:26:55.036
I suppose we're both
refugees, in a way.

00:26:55.113 --> 00:26:58.742
I'm still counting
on getting this ship home.

00:26:58.817 --> 00:27:02.150
Are you sure you'll be
welcome when you do?

00:27:02.220 --> 00:27:05.519
I came across something
else in your database...

00:27:05.590 --> 00:27:08.184
the "Prime Directive."

00:27:08.259 --> 00:27:10.386
The Federation's
"Cardinal Protocol."

00:27:10.462 --> 00:27:11.451
It seems

00:27:11.529 --> 00:27:14.191
you violated it when you
rescued these telepaths.

00:27:14.265 --> 00:27:17.428
Well, let's just say I usually
go with my instincts...

00:27:17.502 --> 00:27:20.027
and sort it out later
at the Board of Inquiry.

00:27:20.105 --> 00:27:23.370
Those Admirals and I were
on a first-name basis, you know.

00:27:23.441 --> 00:27:25.375
Ah.

00:27:25.443 --> 00:27:28.571
You're risking a lot, too.
Why?

00:27:31.549 --> 00:27:33.244
Three months ago,

00:27:33.318 --> 00:27:36.481
my teams were inspecting
a plasma-refining vessel.

00:27:36.554 --> 00:27:38.454
We found a family of telepaths

00:27:38.523 --> 00:27:40.923
hiding in one
of the extraction tanks.

00:27:40.992 --> 00:27:43.392
There was a child...
very young.

00:27:43.461 --> 00:27:48.228
She'd been inside it for days,
barely able to breathe.

00:27:48.299 --> 00:27:52.633
When I lifted her out
and set her down on the deck...

00:27:52.704 --> 00:27:55.571
she thanked me.

00:27:55.640 --> 00:27:58.632
I sent her to a relocation
center with the others,

00:27:58.710 --> 00:28:03.010
knowing full well
what would happen to her.

00:28:03.081 --> 00:28:06.539
After that, I could think
of nothing else,

00:28:06.618 --> 00:28:09.314
and when I couldn't
stand it any longer...

00:28:11.523 --> 00:28:14.549
You're my deliverance, Captain.

00:28:14.626 --> 00:28:16.651
Analysis complete.

00:28:26.037 --> 00:28:27.902
It worked.

00:28:28.039 --> 00:28:31.236
It looks like it'll appear
in about three days...

00:28:31.309 --> 00:28:33.800
less than eight light-years
from here.

00:28:33.878 --> 00:28:34.810
The Tehara system.

00:28:34.879 --> 00:28:35.811
Is that a problem?

00:28:35.880 --> 00:28:37.575
There's an automated
sensor array

00:28:37.649 --> 00:28:38.911
between here and Tehara.

00:28:38.983 --> 00:28:40.041
Can we go around it?

00:28:40.118 --> 00:28:41.551
We'd never make it in time.

00:28:41.619 --> 00:28:43.917
We'll have to find a way
to avoid detection.

00:28:44.022 --> 00:28:46.490
Let's do it in the morning.

00:28:46.558 --> 00:28:49.152
We've done enough for tonight.

00:28:53.331 --> 00:28:55.060
Are you saying good-bye?

00:28:55.133 --> 00:28:58.102
There'll be other spirals.

00:28:58.169 --> 00:29:02.902
They've just never looked
quite so... beautiful before.

00:29:04.876 --> 00:29:07.344
Could be the company
I'm keeping.

00:29:07.412 --> 00:29:09.573
Or the polarization
axis of the windows.

00:29:09.647 --> 00:29:12.172
That must be it.

00:29:15.153 --> 00:29:17.781
How often does this array
emit a scanning pulse?

00:29:17.856 --> 00:29:18.880
Every 40 seconds.

00:29:19.023 --> 00:29:19.887
Range?

00:29:20.024 --> 00:29:21.491
Ten light-years.

00:29:21.559 --> 00:29:22.890
The pulse is designed

00:29:23.027 --> 00:29:26.019
to track warp fields
and impulse signatures.

00:29:26.097 --> 00:29:27.655
If we lower our power output

00:29:27.732 --> 00:29:29.757
to beneath its
detection threshold...

00:29:29.834 --> 00:29:31.734
We could drift past undetected.

00:29:31.803 --> 00:29:33.168
It's worth a try.

00:29:37.575 --> 00:29:40.100
Well, good night.

00:29:40.178 --> 00:29:41.805
Captain...

00:29:41.880 --> 00:29:43.040
why don't you...

00:29:44.115 --> 00:29:45.673
join me?

00:29:45.750 --> 00:29:48.378
I've been looking forward
to trying your replicator.

00:29:48.453 --> 00:29:50.614
Well, I'm sure that I can
come up with something

00:29:50.688 --> 00:29:51.746
to toast the evening.

00:29:51.823 --> 00:29:53.723
We've accomplished
quite a bit today.

00:29:53.792 --> 00:29:55.521
I'm afraid
that won't be possible.

00:29:55.593 --> 00:29:57.527
I had your replicator
taken off-line.

00:29:57.595 --> 00:30:00.723
In case I decided
to replicate a weapon.

00:30:00.799 --> 00:30:02.767
A safety precaution,
you understand.

00:30:02.834 --> 00:30:05.234
Better than anyone.

00:30:05.303 --> 00:30:06.793
Sleep well.

00:30:07.872 --> 00:30:08.861
And you.

00:30:14.245 --> 00:30:15.678
As you were.

00:30:26.791 --> 00:30:27.849
15 seconds.

00:30:27.926 --> 00:30:31.726
Our power output is below
the detection threshold.

00:30:31.796 --> 00:30:33.024
Ten seconds.

00:30:36.868 --> 00:30:38.699
Five... four...

00:30:38.770 --> 00:30:39.964
three...

00:30:40.104 --> 00:30:41.196
two...

00:30:45.877 --> 00:30:47.538
We weren't detected.

00:30:47.612 --> 00:30:49.307
Ten minutes
and we'll be out of range.

00:30:49.380 --> 00:30:52.247
Engineering to Bridge.
We've got a problem.

00:30:52.317 --> 00:30:54.683
That pulse triggered a variance
in the antimatter stream.

00:30:54.752 --> 00:30:56.845
It's not much, but it'll
light us up like a beacon

00:30:56.921 --> 00:30:57.945
when the next pulse hits.

00:30:58.022 --> 00:30:58.954
Options?

00:30:59.023 --> 00:31:00.183
I can't correct it in time.

00:31:00.258 --> 00:31:02.886
So that leaves shutting down
the core.

00:31:02.961 --> 00:31:03.893
Do it.

00:31:03.962 --> 00:31:04.826
The array has released

00:31:04.896 --> 00:31:06.124
- another pulse.
- Time?

00:31:06.197 --> 00:31:07.289
28 seconds.

00:31:07.365 --> 00:31:08.855
Get down
to the plasma injectors.

00:31:08.933 --> 00:31:11.265
Grab a tricorder
and monitor the antimatter flow.

00:31:11.336 --> 00:31:12.303
Aye, sir.

00:31:15.373 --> 00:31:16.271
20 seconds.

00:31:16.341 --> 00:31:17.774
B'Elanna...

00:31:17.842 --> 00:31:18.900
Almost there, Captain.

00:31:18.977 --> 00:31:20.604
I'm having a problem
with the injectors.

00:31:20.678 --> 00:31:22.270
15 seconds.

00:31:24.649 --> 00:31:26.241
Ten seconds.

00:31:30.889 --> 00:31:34.290
Four... three... two...

00:31:38.997 --> 00:31:39.929
We've been detected.

00:31:39.998 --> 00:31:41.625
The array's transmitting
an alert.

00:31:41.699 --> 00:31:43.098
Can we block it?

00:31:43.167 --> 00:31:43.792
Negative.

00:31:43.868 --> 00:31:45.096
Stand down grey mode.

00:31:45.169 --> 00:31:46.796
B'Elanna, fire up the core.

00:31:46.871 --> 00:31:48.429
We're getting out of here.

00:31:48.506 --> 00:31:50.269
Warships will be on their way,

00:31:50.341 --> 00:31:52.468
but we can still
reach the wormhole.

00:31:52.543 --> 00:31:53.601
If we can find it.

00:31:53.678 --> 00:31:55.771
Tom, how long
to the Tehara system?

00:31:55.847 --> 00:31:57.747
11 hours at maximum warp.

00:31:57.815 --> 00:31:59.646
Engines are back on line.

00:31:59.717 --> 00:32:00.877
Engage.

00:32:06.090 --> 00:32:07.489
Using the model we developed,

00:32:07.558 --> 00:32:08.923
we were able to narrow
down the location

00:32:09.027 --> 00:32:11.120
of the wormhole's next
appearance to a radius

00:32:11.195 --> 00:32:12.560
of 200,000 kilometers.

00:32:12.630 --> 00:32:14.029
We can't determine

00:32:14.098 --> 00:32:16.293
its exact position
until we reach the system,

00:32:16.367 --> 00:32:18.597
but we know it will open
in roughly six hours.

00:32:18.670 --> 00:32:21.070
And will remain open
for two minutes at most.

00:32:21.139 --> 00:32:22.868
I've devised
a new shield modulation,

00:32:22.941 --> 00:32:25.102
which should protect us
against their weapons.

00:32:25.176 --> 00:32:26.108
You're not planning

00:32:26.177 --> 00:32:27.872
to fight your way
to the wormhole?

00:32:27.946 --> 00:32:29.208
If I have to.

00:32:29.280 --> 00:32:31.305
Bridge to Captain Janeway.

00:32:31.382 --> 00:32:32.406
Go ahead.

00:32:32.483 --> 00:32:34.417
Long-range sensors have
picked up two Devore warships

00:32:34.485 --> 00:32:35.952
heading right for us.

00:32:36.087 --> 00:32:37.076
Time to intercept?

00:32:37.155 --> 00:32:38.087
Six hours.

00:32:38.156 --> 00:32:39.521
Take the Bridge.
I'll be in Engineering.

00:32:39.590 --> 00:32:40.557
Kashyk.

00:32:42.160 --> 00:32:44.424
First, we'll check those
shield modifications.

00:32:44.495 --> 00:32:46.690
Then we'll see if we
can adjust our phasers

00:32:46.764 --> 00:32:48.356
to penetrate the Devore shields.

00:32:48.433 --> 00:32:50.867
If torpedoes don't work,
I want an alternative.

00:32:50.935 --> 00:32:53.369
Captain, we have to talk

00:32:53.438 --> 00:32:55.133
but not here.

00:33:00.678 --> 00:33:04.910
I'm going back
to rejoin the warships.

00:33:05.016 --> 00:33:07.109
It's the only way that I
can guarantee your safety.

00:33:07.185 --> 00:33:08.117
Kashyk...

00:33:08.186 --> 00:33:09.813
I'm still a ranking officer.

00:33:09.887 --> 00:33:12.412
I can take command
of the inspection teams,

00:33:12.490 --> 00:33:14.890
make sure the refugees
aren't discovered.

00:33:14.959 --> 00:33:16.290
You said yourself
they're suspicious.

00:33:16.361 --> 00:33:17.555
Return now and you
risk being caught.

00:33:17.628 --> 00:33:18.754
I can keep them off track

00:33:18.830 --> 00:33:21.230
long enough to get you
through that wormhole.

00:33:21.299 --> 00:33:22.357
It's too dangerous.

00:33:22.433 --> 00:33:23.627
Kathryn...

00:33:23.701 --> 00:33:25.430
You asked for safe passage
and I agreed,

00:33:25.503 --> 00:33:27.630
under the condition
that you follow my orders.

00:33:27.705 --> 00:33:30.299
You may stand a chance
against one of our warships,

00:33:30.375 --> 00:33:31.364
but not against two.

00:33:31.442 --> 00:33:34.377
If I stay, your best chance
of escape will be lost.

00:33:38.583 --> 00:33:40.915
I could confine you to quarters.

00:33:42.186 --> 00:33:44.814
I was planning on asking you
to stay with us,

00:33:44.889 --> 00:33:46.857
once we got through
the wormhole.

00:33:46.924 --> 00:33:49.119
I wouldn't mind having
someone around

00:33:49.193 --> 00:33:52.253
who appreciates a bit
of Tchaikovsky now and then.

00:33:52.330 --> 00:33:55.629
Generous, but...

00:33:55.700 --> 00:33:58.965
something tells me I wouldn't
fit in any better on Voyager.

00:33:59.070 --> 00:34:01.197
Well...

00:34:01.272 --> 00:34:03.797
you wouldn't be
the first wayward soul

00:34:03.875 --> 00:34:05.843
we've folded into our ranks.

00:34:08.980 --> 00:34:12.609
Your shuttle will be ready
for launch within the hour.

00:34:20.224 --> 00:34:22.852
Our course will put us
just outside the Teharan system

00:34:22.927 --> 00:34:24.451
by the time
the warships arrive.

00:34:24.529 --> 00:34:26.724
Your inspection teams
have to be off Voyager

00:34:26.798 --> 00:34:28.129
before that wormhole opens.

00:34:28.199 --> 00:34:30.895
Believe me, it'll be the
quickest inspection on record.

00:34:30.968 --> 00:34:32.060
I'll be on the Bridge.

00:34:32.136 --> 00:34:34.127
Your efforts have been
greatly appreciated.

00:34:34.205 --> 00:34:36.173
My pleasure.

00:34:36.240 --> 00:34:38.504
Live long and prosper.

00:34:38.576 --> 00:34:40.043
Thank you.

00:34:49.954 --> 00:34:52.445
Begin preignition sequence.

00:34:55.860 --> 00:34:57.987
I've made one adjustment
to your plan.

00:34:59.063 --> 00:35:00.928
After the inspection,
we're going to wait

00:35:00.998 --> 00:35:02.829
at the wormhole
for as long as we can...

00:35:02.900 --> 00:35:04.800
until it begins to collapse.

00:35:04.869 --> 00:35:07.565
I may not be able
to join you this time.

00:35:07.638 --> 00:35:09.401
Try.

00:36:28.819 --> 00:36:30.548
They're assuming
a tactical formation.

00:36:30.621 --> 00:36:31.588
Shields?

00:36:31.656 --> 00:36:33.146
No. We follow protocol.

00:36:33.224 --> 00:36:35.021
Bridge to Transporter Room.

00:36:35.092 --> 00:36:36.320
Status?

00:36:36.394 --> 00:36:38.555
Ready, Captain.
Pattern cohesion stable.

00:36:38.629 --> 00:36:39.755
Cargo Bay 1?

00:36:39.830 --> 00:36:40.762
Clear.

00:36:40.831 --> 00:36:41.798
They're hailing.

00:36:41.866 --> 00:36:43.299
On screen.

00:36:43.367 --> 00:36:45.198
Gaharay vessel,
prepare to be...

00:36:45.269 --> 00:36:47.931
We've been through
three inspections.

00:36:48.005 --> 00:36:49.768
Please explain
why another is necessary.

00:36:49.840 --> 00:36:52.400
Crew members are instructed to
step away from their stations.

00:36:52.476 --> 00:36:56.242
Side arms and scanning equipment
are to be set aside.

00:36:56.314 --> 00:36:57.941
Deviation from this
or any other

00:36:58.015 --> 00:37:00.779
inspection protocols
will not be tolerated.

00:37:00.851 --> 00:37:02.648
All hands, this is the Captain.

00:37:02.720 --> 00:37:05.621
Prepare to be boarded
by Devore inspection teams.

00:37:05.690 --> 00:37:07.624
Give them
your usual warm welcome.

00:37:07.692 --> 00:37:10.320
Devore soldiers
have materialized

00:37:10.394 --> 00:37:12.988
on Decks 15, 12, 8, 4...

00:37:13.064 --> 00:37:14.861
And... 1.

00:37:16.534 --> 00:37:20.265
Captain Janeway,
report to your ready room.

00:37:24.408 --> 00:37:26.774
Captain.

00:37:26.844 --> 00:37:28.903
Good to see you again.

00:37:28.980 --> 00:37:30.607
Likewise.

00:37:59.844 --> 00:38:00.868
Tchaikovsky.

00:38:00.945 --> 00:38:03.539
Of all the selections
in your database,

00:38:03.614 --> 00:38:05.980
this remains my favorite.

00:38:06.050 --> 00:38:07.779
Mine, too.

00:38:07.852 --> 00:38:10.343
I'm afraid Prax isn't impressed.

00:38:10.421 --> 00:38:13.652
He's solely concerned
with his work, aren't you, Prax?

00:38:13.724 --> 00:38:14.884
As you say, sir.

00:38:15.026 --> 00:38:17.460
Yes, he's curious why
you entered this sector.

00:38:17.528 --> 00:38:18.995
You're aware it's restricted.

00:38:19.063 --> 00:38:20.360
We were planning to study

00:38:20.431 --> 00:38:22.524
a supernova remnant
not far from here.

00:38:22.600 --> 00:38:24.693
You strayed a full light-year
from your course

00:38:24.769 --> 00:38:26.896
in order to observe
an astronomical phenomenon?

00:38:27.038 --> 00:38:28.403
We're explorers.

00:38:28.472 --> 00:38:29.404
Yes, I remember.

00:38:29.473 --> 00:38:30.804
I also remember warning you

00:38:30.875 --> 00:38:32.706
about going
where you don't belong.

00:38:32.777 --> 00:38:37.578
Exploring can sometimes
be hard to resist, Inspector.

00:38:37.648 --> 00:38:40.173
Well, it's a romantic notion,
Captain,

00:38:40.251 --> 00:38:42.845
but one I can't allow you
to indulge.

00:38:42.920 --> 00:38:46.617
I'm afraid I'll have to ask you
to leave our space immediately.

00:38:46.691 --> 00:38:48.090
Prax, why don't you check

00:38:48.159 --> 00:38:50.559
on our teams, while I reiterate

00:38:50.628 --> 00:38:53.358
our protocols
for Captain Janeway.

00:38:58.102 --> 00:38:59.535
Do they suspect anything?

00:38:59.603 --> 00:39:00.865
Not yet,

00:39:00.938 --> 00:39:02.200
but our warships

00:39:02.273 --> 00:39:04.298
have been monitoring
Voyager's movements

00:39:04.375 --> 00:39:06.309
for the past few days,
and mine as well.

00:39:06.377 --> 00:39:07.867
I don't think we have much time.

00:39:07.945 --> 00:39:08.877
The Brenari?

00:39:08.979 --> 00:39:10.776
They're in transporter
suspension.

00:39:10.848 --> 00:39:12.406
And the wormhole?

00:39:12.483 --> 00:39:14.007
We found it.

00:39:14.085 --> 00:39:16.349
It's 20,000 kilometers
off our port bow.

00:39:16.420 --> 00:39:18.581
We've determined
that a photon torpedo,

00:39:18.656 --> 00:39:21.352
properly calibrated,
will force open the threshold

00:39:21.425 --> 00:39:23.552
long enough for Voyager
to get through.

00:39:23.627 --> 00:39:26.892
Congratulations, Captain.

00:39:26.997 --> 00:39:30.865
For awhile, I wasn't sure
if even you could find it.

00:39:30.935 --> 00:39:32.368
Prax.

00:39:35.506 --> 00:39:38.805
Go to Cargo Bay 1.

00:39:38.876 --> 00:39:40.138
You'll find
the transporter patterns

00:39:40.211 --> 00:39:41.769
for more than a dozen telepaths.

00:39:41.846 --> 00:39:43.245
Rematerialize them.

00:39:43.314 --> 00:39:44.542
Yes, sir.

00:39:45.716 --> 00:39:47.877
Impressive.

00:39:47.952 --> 00:39:50.785
You gave
a masterful performance.

00:39:50.855 --> 00:39:53.346
I'm the one who's impressed

00:39:53.424 --> 00:39:56.916
with your selflessness,
your humanity.

00:39:57.061 --> 00:40:00.087
It made all this so much easier.

00:40:00.164 --> 00:40:02.632
Oh, but what about
your selflessness?

00:40:02.700 --> 00:40:05.601
That touching story
about the little girl...

00:40:05.669 --> 00:40:07.637
was that a fabrication, too?

00:40:07.705 --> 00:40:09.502
Oh, that incident was real.

00:40:09.573 --> 00:40:11.063
What I didn't tell you

00:40:11.142 --> 00:40:13.838
was that after wrestling
with my ethics,

00:40:13.911 --> 00:40:16.641
I realized that I'd
done the right thing

00:40:16.714 --> 00:40:20.343
in order to protect my people
from a very real threat.

00:40:20.418 --> 00:40:21.908
Please.

00:40:28.025 --> 00:40:29.720
I insist.

00:40:58.122 --> 00:40:59.714
Captain...

00:41:05.796 --> 00:41:07.559
Access their forward
sensor array.

00:41:07.631 --> 00:41:10.191
You should find
neutrino emissions

00:41:10.267 --> 00:41:13.862
at roughly 20,000 kilometers
off the port bow.

00:41:13.938 --> 00:41:15.235
On screen.

00:41:19.109 --> 00:41:20.406
Target two photon torpedoes.

00:41:20.478 --> 00:41:24.574
When the first one detonates,
the wormhole will open.

00:41:24.648 --> 00:41:28.049
Use the second one to
destabilize its subspace matrix.

00:41:28.118 --> 00:41:30.052
That will destroy it.

00:41:30.120 --> 00:41:32.054
Prax, report.

00:41:32.122 --> 00:41:34.556
I've isolated the bio-patterns.

00:41:45.503 --> 00:41:47.095
Fire.

00:41:53.177 --> 00:41:55.771
It should have detonated.

00:41:57.114 --> 00:41:58.741
Those aren't neutrino emissions.

00:41:58.816 --> 00:42:00.716
They're antimatter
residue signatures.

00:42:00.784 --> 00:42:02.945
There's no wormhole here.

00:42:05.689 --> 00:42:07.748
You created false readings.

00:42:07.825 --> 00:42:11.192
That is the theme
for this evening, isn't it?

00:42:12.329 --> 00:42:15.093
Prax, do you have the telepaths?

00:42:15.165 --> 00:42:17.326
I have cargo containers...

00:42:20.971 --> 00:42:23.269
filled with vegetables.

00:42:25.776 --> 00:42:27.437
Return to the Bridge.

00:42:27.511 --> 00:42:29.274
Computer,
change music selection.

00:42:29.346 --> 00:42:31.940
Mahler's Symphony #1,
second movement.

00:42:32.049 --> 00:42:33.778
Maybe this will help you relax.

00:42:33.851 --> 00:42:37.343
Inspector, we've completed
our inventory of the vessel.

00:42:37.421 --> 00:42:39.355
Two of their shuttlecraft
are missing.

00:42:39.423 --> 00:42:40.890
They couldn't have gone far.

00:42:40.958 --> 00:42:43.392
Why didn't they appear
on our long-range scans?

00:42:43.460 --> 00:42:44.757
Of course!

00:42:44.828 --> 00:42:47.092
Adjust their scanners
to compensate

00:42:47.164 --> 00:42:48.927
for refractive shielding.

00:42:48.999 --> 00:42:51.194
Well, you gave us
the specifications.

00:42:51.268 --> 00:42:53.065
Seemed a shame to waste them.

00:42:53.137 --> 00:42:55.970
We've located
the two shuttlecraft.

00:42:56.040 --> 00:42:58.406
Range 20 million kilometers.

00:42:58.475 --> 00:43:00.739
Order our ships to pursue.

00:43:00.811 --> 00:43:02.005
Maximum speed!

00:43:04.582 --> 00:43:06.072
We're approaching
the coordinates.

00:43:06.150 --> 00:43:07.947
I'm firing the torpedo.

00:43:22.533 --> 00:43:24.228
The shuttles have disappeared
from sensors.

00:43:24.301 --> 00:43:25.495
We've scanned for a wormhole.

00:43:25.569 --> 00:43:28.595
If there was one, it's gone.

00:43:29.840 --> 00:43:32.638
I'll order Janeway
and her crew removed.

00:43:32.710 --> 00:43:34.644
We'll confiscate the vessel,

00:43:34.712 --> 00:43:37.909
deliver them to the nearest
detention center.

00:43:37.982 --> 00:43:39.210
You're dismissed.

00:43:40.351 --> 00:43:41.943
Imperative 12, Codicil Six
requires...

00:43:42.086 --> 00:43:44.213
To hell with protocol, Prax!

00:43:44.288 --> 00:43:46.552
Do you think
either of us will benefit

00:43:46.624 --> 00:43:48.683
from having this failure
on our records?

00:43:48.759 --> 00:43:52.718
As far as you're concerned,
this incident never occurred.

00:43:52.796 --> 00:43:56.288
Make sure your teams share
that understanding.

00:44:11.048 --> 00:44:13.778
Well played, Captain.

00:44:13.851 --> 00:44:16.718
It seems I never did
earn your trust.

00:44:16.787 --> 00:44:19.085
I had to take a few precautions.

00:44:19.156 --> 00:44:20.248
You understand.

00:44:20.324 --> 00:44:22.588
Better than anyone.

00:44:22.660 --> 00:44:23.854
I never lied to you.

00:44:23.927 --> 00:44:26.361
My offer to take you with us
was genuine,

00:44:26.430 --> 00:44:27.897
and it would still stand

00:44:27.965 --> 00:44:30.365
if you'd kept
your part of the bargain.

00:44:31.435 --> 00:44:34.336
For what it's worth...

00:44:34.405 --> 00:44:37.932
you made a tempting offer.

00:44:43.080 --> 00:44:45.844
The Bridge is yours.
